5\. Caching & Cache-Aside
=========================

  

Caching stores frequently accessed data in a faster storage layer.

  

    Client  ↓Node.js  ↓Redis  ↓ cache missMongoDB

  

### Cache-aside

  

Most common strategy:

  

JavaScript

    const cached = await redis.get(key);if (cached) {    return JSON.parse(cached);}const data = await db.find(...);await redis.set(key, JSON.stringify(data), {    EX: 300});return data;

  

Flow:

  

    Read cache   ↓Hit → return   ↓Miss   ↓Database   ↓Store in cache   ↓Return

  

### Problem

  

**Cache invalidation.**

  

When database changes:

  

    UPDATE MongoDBDELETE Redis cache

  

