6\. Redis & Cache Eviction
==========================

  

Redis is an in-memory data store commonly used for:

  

  
*     
    
    caching
    
      
    
  
*     
    
    sessions
    
      
    
  
*     
    
    rate limiting
    
      
    
  
*     
    
    distributed locks
    
      
    
  
*     
    
    counters
    
      
    
  
*     
    
    queues
    
      
    
  
*     
    
    pub/sub
    
      
    
  

  

### Cache eviction

  

What happens when Redis memory is full?

  

Policies include:

  

    LRULFUTTL-based expiration

  

### LRU

  

Least Recently Used.

  

Remove data that hasn't been accessed recently.

  

### LFU

  

Least Frequently Used.

  

Remove data that is accessed least often.

  

