7\. Database Indexing & Transactions
====================================

  

Index
-----

  

An index makes searching faster.

  

Without index:

  

    MongoDB scans documents

  

With index:

  

    Index → matching document

  

Example:

  

JavaScript

    db.users.createIndex({ email: 1 })

  

Then:

  

JavaScript

    db.users.findOne({ email: "abc@gmail.com" })

  

can use the index.

  

### Trade-off

  

Indexes improve reads but:

  

  
*     
    
    consume memory/disk
    
      
    
  
*     
    
    slow writes
    
      
    
  
*     
    
    require maintenance
    
      
    
  

  

**Interview question:**

  

>   
> 
> Should we index every field?
> 
>   

  

**No.**

  

Indexes have a cost, and unnecessary indexes can hurt write performance.

  

* * *

  

Transactions
------------

  

A transaction makes multiple operations behave as one logical operation.

  

Example:

  

    Transfer ₹100Account A - ₹100Account B + ₹100

  

We don't want:

  

    A = -100B = unchanged

  

Transaction gives atomicity.

  

MongoDB supports multi-document transactions.

  

